{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790998383,"nonce":"GuNY6NoAqsm1YHtkwdAVMUkCl3Q=","message":"Fixed in 6296521 without changing Blinc: every LayoutTree handle is a view onto one Blinc tree for the process, so node ids are unique across all of them and no write or binding can reach another handle's node. A handle owns the nodes it created; dispose removes them at once, collection at the next flush. One flush applies the whole queue to the shared tree. Memory: tree-dispose now plateaus at about 112 MB (was flat at 94 MB with per-handle trees; the shared maps keep their capacity), tree, color, signal and computed unchanged. A future cost: release_handle scans the owner map, so disposing a tree is linear in all live nodes; a per-handle node set would make it linear in its own.","files":null}]}